{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1339260-did-anyone-else-find-this-really-distracting-\u201csir\u201d-in-the-tormented-real","id":1339260,"title":"Did anyone else find this really distracting? \u201csir\u201d in The Tormented real","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-03T16:34:22-07:00","id":1339260,"title":"Did anyone else find this really distracting? \u201csir\u201d in The Tormented real","content":"I get that they\u2019re nonbinary characters, but couldn\u2019t you just use \u201cthey\u201d and \u201cthem\u201d?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T16:35:23-07:00","id":1339261,"title":"","content":"I meant the use of the pronouns \u201czie\u201d and \u201czir\u201d in The Tormented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T16:45:09-07:00","id":1339264,"title":"","content":"Yes, I found it distracting and difficult to parse.<br /> No, I'm not convinced that's a good reason not to have done it.<br /> <br /> To be honest, at launch, this really bothered me, but I've since done some reflection and honestly couldn't explain why it bothered me so much. So I've reconsidered my feelings on it - if the cost of social change is a little distraction when reading through books tied to my hobby, I'll pay it gladly.<br /> <br /> Whether or not the chosen language was the correct approach, and the advantages it may or may not have over 'they/them' (which I've seen used in more recent works, and which would have been easier to parse), I can't speak to because I'm, frankly, uninformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T18:36:02-07:00","id":1339284,"title":"","content":"Like any new word, it takes some getting used to. I stumbled over it in when it was used in Prommie 2nd, but it's popped up in more and more books since and I just start flowing with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T19:39:46-07:00","id":1339294,"title":"","content":"Distracting? Yeah, a little at first. Rules we grow up with are The Rules, The Way Things Are, and as far as we know when we're young, The Way Things Have Always Been. Those habits that are so deep we don't even think of them as habits because we don't think of there being any other way to do things? They're comfortable. Not having to think about something is easier than actively thinking about it, and it gets to the point where changing is downright *un*comfortable. Like exercising a muscle that's gotten used to only ever doing the bare minimum. But just like a muscle the more you work with it the less you notice and the more comfortable it gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T21:55:12-07:00","id":1339307,"title":"","content":"It's good practice to see them in print, because they do help your brain normalize their use. &quot;They&quot; is fine up until a person's pronouns are established, but it isn't fine to continue to use it if something else is preferred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T00:53:53-07:00","id":1339315,"title":"","content":"Ahaha, I consider it a sign of progress that peeps would rather see they/them. Coulda been asking for she or he.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:55:51-07:00","id":1339360,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answering <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't know any nonbinary people irl, and only a couple online. I'm just not used to the pronouns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}